    <item>
      <title>Process Injection - AV Evasion</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/process-injection-av-evasion/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 01 Apr 2026 14:30:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/process-injection-av-evasion/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;In the previous posts, we have explored various techniques for process injection, such as using &lt;code&gt;VirtualAllocEx&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;CreateRemoteThread&lt;/code&gt;. However, these methods often require write and execute permissions on the target process, which can trigger antivirus (AV) detection. In this article, we will create shellcode using the Process Injection technique combined with XOR encryption to obfuscate the code and evade antivirus detection. By encrypting our shellcode, we can make it less recognizable to AV software, which often relies on signature-based detection methods.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Process Injection without Write/Execute Permission</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/process-injection-without-wx-permission/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 01 Apr 2026 13:30:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/process-injection-without-wx-permission/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;In the previous post, we discussed the Self Injection method, which allows us to inject shellcode into a process and execute it. However, this method requires write and execute permissions on the memory where the shellcode is injected. In this post, we will explore how to perform process injection without requiring write/execute permissions.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Create a payload using Shellcode in C language targeting a 64-bit machine.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div&#xA;  class=&#34;code-block-container border-border bg-card my-6 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border shadow-sm transition-all duration-200 ease-out hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:shadow-md&#34;&#xA;  data-code-block&#xA;  data-code-id=&#34;code-0&#34;&#xA;  data-collapsible=&#34;true&#34;&#xA;  data-default-state=&#34;expanded&#34;&#xA;  data-collapsed=&#34;false&#34;&#xA;  data-auto-collapse-lines=&#34;30&#34;&#xA;  data-auto-collapse-height=&#34;400&#34;&#xA;  data-collapsed-height=&#34;120&#34;&#xA;&gt;&#xA;  &#xA;  &lt;div&#xA;    class=&#34;code-block-header bg-muted/30 border-border flex items-center justify-between border-b px-4 py-3&#34;&#xA;  &gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;flex items-center gap-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;div class=&#34;text-muted-foreground shrink-0&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;svg class=&#34;h-4 w-4&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;path stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; d=&#34;M10 20l4-16m4 4l4 4-4 4M6 16l-4-4 4-4&#34; /&gt;&#xA;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;      &lt;span class=&#34;text-muted-foreground text-sm font-medium&#34;&gt;&#xA;        TERMINAL&#xA;      &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;flex items-center gap-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;button&#xA;          class=&#34;collapse-code-btn text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary hover:bg-primar