    <item>
      <title>Process Injection - Self Injection Method</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/process-injection-self-injection-method/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 31 Mar 2026 13:30:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/process-injection-self-injection-method/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Self Injection is a technique that allows an attacker to inject shellcode into a process and execute it. This method is often used in malware development and can be used to bypass security measures. The basic idea is to create a new thread in the target process and execute the shellcode in that thread.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Below is an example of how to create a payload using Shellcode in C language targeting a 64-bit machine.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
